NAME
       traceroute - show the routers on the way to a host

SYNOPSIS
       traceroute [-n] HOST

DESCRIPTION
       traceroute sends test packets with a growing "time to live", so that
       each router on the way to HOST in turn answers that the packet expired.
       It prints one line per router (hop) with three answer times. A * means
       no answer arrived for that try.

       traceroute is in its own package; tracepath, from iputils, does almost
       the same and is always installed.

OPTIONS
       -n     Print addresses only; do not look up names.

EXAMPLES
           traceroute -n utility.lab.example.com

SEE ALSO
       tracepath(8), ping(8), ip(8)
